diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1a55755..caf4059 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,7 +6,25 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": <string or null>}`: one page
+  of items, ordered by `id` ascending.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
+### `GET /items` query parameters
+
+- `limit`: integer from 1 to 100, default 20.
+- `cursor`: opaque string copied from a previous response's `next_cursor`.
+  Omit it for the first page. Pass it back unchanged.
+
+Walk the list by repeating the request with `next_cursor` until it is `null`.
+`next_cursor` is `null` on the last page, which may hold fewer items than `limit`.
+
+The cursor is the base64url encoding (with padding) of the `id` of the last item
+on the previous page. Clients must treat it as opaque; the encoding may change.
+
+### Errors
+
+A bad `limit` (not an integer, or outside 1 to 100) or a malformed `cursor`
+returns status 400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
+
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
